    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nWhen the border is activated, the floating window can end up positioned behind the popup menu.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Ensure that the floating window has the border enabled.\r\n2. Type text until the popup menu appears.\r\n3. Ensure that the floating window, with an enabled border, is opened near the end of the Neovim window.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI subtracted 2 from the width of the floating window to account for the 2 columns added by the border. This adjustment could be applied only when the border is active.\r\n\r\n![after](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91300213/540dce82-ccbd-45d0-aea1-261782142c8e)\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n![before](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91300213/2543bcfd-49c4-4938-be13-d6692aa00f7d)",
